        name = "Tabard of the Achiever",
        stepCount = 8,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Collect twenty-five distinct tabards using current vendors and reputation rewards.\n\n1. Track Twenty-Five Tabards (1021) and note its counter. Work from the number already credited; the number of Wardrobe appearances is not a reliable substitute.\n\n2. Start with inexpensive purchases: your faction's city tabards, Guild Tabard, and Private's Tabard plus Knight's Colors for Alliance, or Scout's Tabard plus Stone Guard's Herald for Horde. The PvP pair costs Marks of Honor, not removed battleground tokens.\n\n3. Use the individual city-tabard guides in this catalogue for current sellers and maps. Buy and equip each different tabard, checking 1021 after each purchase. Repeated copies of the same item add nothing.\n\n4. Add the four Wrath reputation tabards: Argent Crusade, Ebon Blade, Wyrmrest Accord and Kirin Tor. Each requires Friendly, not Exalted. Their guides explain the Shadow Vault unlock and each separate quartermaster.\n\n5. Fill the remaining count with tabards whose requirements you already meet. Outland's Honor Hold/Thrallmar, Cenarion Expedition, Lower City, Sha'tar and other reputation rewards are useful choices; use their individual guides for the Exalted grinds. Green and Purple Trophy Tabards of the Illidari and Tabard of the Explorer provide more options. A retired event reward is unnecessary.\n\n6. Equip each new tabard and recheck the counter. Relog if credit is delayed. Keep required purchases; old comments promising permanent credit after refunding PvP or tournament tabards are not a dependable shopping plan.\n\n7. At 25 credited tabards, collect the mailed reward. For missing mail or an alt's physical copy, speak to Elizabeth Ross in Northrend Dalaran (51.6, 55.4), Rebecca Laughlin in Stormwind (64.0, 77.2), or Garyl in Orgrimmar (47.5, 75.5). Choose the lost-Tabard-of-the-Achiever dialogue; it is not ordinary vendor stock.\n\n8. Equip the reward and confirm the appearance. Once the achievement is earned, eligible alts can use that recovery dialogue without collecting 25 tabards again.",
