        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Discover every required subzone across the nine Northrend exploration achievements.\n\n1. Track Northrend Explorer (45). Open its nine zone achievements to see missing named areas. Fly into each actual area until discovery credit appears; passing far above or beside it can miss the trigger.\n\n2. Borean Tundra: start near the Transitus Shield in Coldarra (33.2, 34.4), cover the island, then the mainland's missing areas. Howling Fjord: use the Utgarde approach (57.3, 46.7) as a central reference and cover the missing coast, islands and inland areas. Select each zone separately in the dropdown.\n\n3. Dragonblight: start from Wyrmrest Temple (59.8, 53.0) and visit missing dragonshrines and settlements. Grizzly Hills: use Camp Oneqwah (64.8, 46.8) as a reference and cover its missing areas. Exploration does not require talking to or fighting the local faction NPCs.\n\n4. Zul'Drak: start near Ebon Watch (14.0, 73.8), then cover the terraces and missing temples. Sholazar Basin: start at Nesingwary Base Camp (27.0, 58.6) and visit every missing lake, pillar and camp area.\n\n5. The Storm Peaks: start at K3 (41.0, 86.0), then explore missing northern and high-altitude areas. Crystalsong Forest: begin below Dalaran near the teleport crystal (15.8, 42.4) and cover the forest's named areas. Dalaran above it does not substitute for Crystalsong exploration.\n\n6. Icecrown: begin at the Argent Vanguard (87.6, 75.6) and fly through the missing named areas. Confirm that Icecrown's exploration achievement and all eight other zones are checked under Northrend Explorer.\n\n7. Collect the mailed tabard; do not chase Brann for a turn-in. For missing mail or an alt's copy, speak to Elizabeth Ross in Northrend Dalaran (51.6, 55.4) and choose the lost-Tabard-of-the-Explorer dialogue. Equip it to confirm the appearance.",
